Package: backgammonr
Type: Package
Title: Thompson-Sampling Toolkit for Finite-Budget Backgammon Decisions
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Gabriel",
           family = "Alwan",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "gabriel.alwan@gmail.com")
Author: Gabriel Alwan [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Gabriel Alwan <gabriel.alwan@gmail.com>
Description: Thompson-sampling research toolkit for fixed-budget best-action
    identification under Monte Carlo noise, with backgammon as a realistic
    stochastic laboratory. The package frames one board state plus one
    realized dice roll as a finite-budget simulation-allocation problem over
    legal root actions. It distinguishes rollout-model values, high-budget
    proxy references, and unavailable game-theoretic truth; keeps sequential
    Thompson sampling as the canonical allocation policy; and provides a
    compact front door for proxy-reference estimation, method comparison,
    evaluation, and visualization.
